            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
            equipped with a Zariski topology. This is the original definition of Zariski topology, and serves well to motivate the concept, but eventually it was superceded by a more refined concept of Zariski topologies of prime spectra, discussed in the next subsection
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#OnAffineVarieties"} below
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AffinSpaceAsPrimeSpectrum"}
            below we reconsider the naive case of interest in this subsection here from that more refined perspective.
